        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What Is a Coroutine",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "==Coroutine==: a function defined with `async def`",
            "Calling it returns a coroutine object and runs **nothing**",
            "Its body runs only once it is awaited or scheduled",
            "==Event loop==: a single-threaded scheduler that runs ready callbacks",
            "Then it polls I/O with a selector (epoll / kqueue / IOCP)"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "async def fetch():",
            "    return 42",
            "c = fetch()  # nothing runs yet",
            "print(c)  # <coroutine object>",
            "asyncio.run(c)  # -> 42"
          ],
          "note": "calling is not running"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. How the Loop Switches",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Condition",
            "Loop action"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`await aw` pending",
              "run next ready task"
            ],
            [
              "`await sleep(0)`",
              "yield **once**, resume"
            ],
            [
              "no await",
              "never switched"
            ],
            [
              "ready queue empty",
              "poll selector I/O"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`asyncio.run(main())` __creates__ a new loop",
            "Runs `main()` until it returns",
            "Cancels any leftover tasks",
            "Shuts down async generators",
            "Closes the loop"
          ],
          "style": "number",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
