      "page_title": "asyncio.Queue: Producer/Consumer",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 1. What is it",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "==asyncio.Queue(maxsize=n)==: a FIFO shared by coroutines",
            "**Not** thread-safe: use it within one event loop only",
            "`maxsize=0` (the default) means **unbounded**",
            "Producers `put`, consumers `get`, in arrival order"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Variant",
            "Order",
            "Item shape"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`Queue`",
              "FIFO",
              "any"
            ],
            [
              "`PriorityQueue`",
              "smallest first",
              "`(priority, item)`"
            ],
            [
              "`LifoQueue`",
              "stack (LIFO)",
              "any"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 2. Mechanism",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Call",
            "When",
            "Result"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`await q.put(x)`",
              "full",
              "**waits**"
            ],
            [
              "`await q.get()`",
              "empty",
              "**waits**"
            ],
            [
              "`put_nowait(x)`",
              "full",
              "raises `QueueFull`"
            ],
            [
              "`get_nowait()`",
              "empty",
              "raises `QueueEmpty`"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A blocking put is ==backpressure==: it slows fast producers down",
            "`q.task_done()`: call it once per processed item",
            "`await q.join()`: waits until every item put is marked done",
            "Counter: +1 on each put, −1 on each task_done, and join waits for 0"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              {
                "text": "Producer",
                "sub": "await put()",
                "ink": "orange"
              },
              {
                "text": "Queue(maxsize)",
                "sub": "full → put waits",
                "ink": "blue"
              },
              {
                "text": "N workers",
                "sub": "await get()",
                "ink": "purple"
              },
              {
                "text": "task_done()",
                "sub": "join() → 0",
                "ink": "green"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "q = asyncio.Queue(maxsize=100)",
            "ws = [create_task(worker(q))",
            "      for _ in range(4)]",
            "for x in items: await q.put(x)",
            "await q.join()   # all done",
            "for w in ws: w.cancel()"
          ],
          "note": "join first, then cancel workers"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 4. Shutdown Options",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Way",
            "How",
            "Catch"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "join + cancel",
              "`join()`, then `w.cancel()`",
              "keep task refs"
            ],
            [
              "Sentinel",
              "one `None` **per worker**",
              "worker checks None"
            ],
            [
              "`q.shutdown()` 3.13+",
              "put/get raise `QueueShutDown`",
              "no sentinels needed"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 2,
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Bounded vs unbounded",
          "text": "Set `maxsize`: put waits and memory stays flat. For Queue vs gather + Semaphore, see page 8."
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Worker sees `None` → returns, no cancel needed",
            "Items queued before the sentinel are ==all processed==",
            "Still call `task_done()` for the None if you `join()`"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "python",
      "subtitle": "FIFO + workers"
