    {
      "page_title": "Queue Workers, Shutdown & PriorityQueue",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 5. Common Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "No `task_done()` in ==finally==, so one exception makes `join()` hang **forever**",
            "Unbounded queue + fast producer: memory grows without limit",
            "One `None` for 4 workers: 3 workers never exit",
            "Sharing the Queue across threads: it is not thread-safe",
            "Cancelling workers **before** `join()` drops queued items"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 3. Template: N Workers",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "async def worker(q):",
            "    while True:",
            "        item = await q.get()",
            "        try: await process(item)",
            "        finally: q.task_done()"
          ],
          "note": "task_done in finally, always"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 6. Sentinel Shutdown",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "for x in items: await q.put(x)",
            "for _ in ws: await q.put(None)",
            "await asyncio.gather(*ws)"
          ],
          "note": "one None per worker"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 7. q.shutdown() (3.13+)",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "async def worker(q):",
            "  try:",
            "    while True:",
            "      await handle(await q.get())",
            "  except asyncio.QueueShutDown:",
            "    return"
          ],
          "note": "producer calls q.shutdown() when done"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "After `shutdown()`, any `put` raises ==QueueShutDown==",
            "`get` drains the remaining items, **then** raises",
            "`shutdown(immediate=True)` drops whatever is left"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 8. PriorityQueue Example",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "pq = asyncio.PriorityQueue()",
            "await pq.put((2, \"email\"))",
            "await pq.put((0, \"page oncall\"))",
            "p, job = await pq.get()",
            "# -> (0, 'page oncall')"
          ],
          "note": "smallest priority comes out first"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Call",
            "Waits?",
            "Use when"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`put` / `get`",
              "yes",
              "normal flow"
            ],
            [
              "`put_nowait`",
              "no, QueueFull",
              "drop on overload"
            ],
            [
              "`get_nowait`",
              "no, QueueEmpty",
              "poll, never block"
            ],
            [
              "`q.qsize()`",
              "no",
              "metrics only"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "☆ 9. Best Practices",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Always bound the queue with `maxsize`",
            "Put `task_done()` inside `finally`",
            "Keep references to every worker task",
            "Size N workers to the ==downstream limit=="
          ],
          "style": "checkbox"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Priority ties",
          "text": "Equal priorities compare the items next, which can raise TypeError. Add a counter: `(prio, n, item)`."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "python",
      "subtitle": "FIFO + workers"
