      "page_title": "Semaphore: Capping Concurrency & Rate",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What is it",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "==asyncio.Semaphore(n)== wraps an internal **counter** that starts at n",
            "`acquire()` decrements it and **waits** while it is 0",
            "`release()` increments it and wakes one waiting task",
            "It caps ==concurrency== (≤ n in flight), __not__ requests/sec"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Mechanism",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "async def fetch(sem, url):",
            "  async with sem: # freed on error",
            "    return await get(url)"
          ],
          "note": "permit released even if get() raises"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Step",
            "counter",
            "action"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "start Semaphore(2)",
              "2",
              "—"
            ],
            [
              "A acquires",
              "1",
              "A runs"
            ],
            [
              "B acquires",
              "0",
              "B runs"
            ],
            [
              "C acquires",
              "0",
              "C **waits**"
            ],
            [
              "A releases",
              "1→0",
              "__C wakes__"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 4,
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Primitive",
            "extra release()"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Semaphore(n)",
              "silent, counter +1"
            ],
            [
              "{green:BoundedSemaphore}",
              "**ValueError**, so leaks show up"
            ],
            [
              "Semaphore(1)",
              "silent → 2 permits!"
            ],
            [
              "Lock",
              "RuntimeError"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "solid"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Example: 1000 URLs",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
