        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Lock: one at a time",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "==asyncio.Lock==: mutual exclusion between coroutines",
            "`async with lock:` guards a critical section containing an `await`",
            "Needed only when an **await** sits between read and write",
            "Pure sync code never interleaves, so it needs no lock",
            "**Not** reentrant: acquiring it twice in one task deadlocks"
          ],
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "lock = asyncio.Lock()",
            "async with lock:",
            "    bal = acct.bal     # read",
            "    await audit(bal)   # yields!",
            "    acct.bal = bal + n # write"
          ],
          "note": "without lock: lost update at await"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Event: broadcast flag",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "==asyncio.Event==: a boolean flag, starts False",
            "`await ev.wait()` blocks until `ev.set()`",
            "`ev.clear()` resets it; `ev.is_set()` checks it",
            "`set()` wakes **ALL** waiters at once: a ==broadcast== signal",
            "Typical: 'server ready', 'shutdown requested'"
          ],
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "ready = asyncio.Event()",
            "async def worker():",
            "    await ready.wait()  # park",
            "    serve()",
            "ready.set()   # wakes every one"
          ],
          "note": "stays set until clear()"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Condition: wait on state",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "==asyncio.Condition== = a Lock + `wait()` / `notify(n)` / `notify_all()`",
            "Waits on a __predicate__, not just a flag",
            "`wait_for(pred)` **re-checks** pred after each wake-up",
            "Must hold the lock: `async with cond:`"
          ],
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "async with cond:  # consumer",
            "    await cond.wait_for(",
            "        lambda: bool(buf))",
            "    item = buf.pop()",
            "async with cond:  # producer",
            "    buf.append(x); cond.notify()"
          ],
          "note": "notify wakes n, not all"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Example: async cache",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "async def get(k):",
            "  async with lock:",
            "    if k not in cache:  # miss",
            "      cache[k] = await load(k)",
            "    return cache[k]"
          ],
          "note": "2nd task waits, then hits cache"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "No lock: 100 tasks miss the same key → 100 fetches",
            "That stampede is the ==thundering herd==",
            "With lock: 1 fetch, 99 tasks read the cache",
            "Refine: one Lock **per key** so other keys don't queue"
          ],
          "style": "star"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Threads? Careful!",
          "text": "asyncio primitives are **not** thread-safe. From another thread, use `loop.call_soon_threadsafe(ev.set)`. Never call `ev.set()` directly."
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Thread callbacks must not touch loop objects directly",
            "`call_soon_threadsafe` ==queues== `set` onto the loop",
            "It also wakes the selector, so the waiter runs promptly"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Pick the smallest tool",
          "text": "One at a time? **Lock**. A signal? **Event**. A state change? **Condition**."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "python",
      "subtitle": "coordinating coroutines"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Sync Primitives Compared & Thread Signals",
      "blocks": [
        {
