            "`await writer.write(x)` raises TypeError because write is **not** a coroutine",
            "`close()` without `await wait_closed()` leaves the socket still closing",
            "Using `read(n)` for fixed frames can return **fewer** bytes",
            "No `if not data` check means you loop forever at EOF"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
